            <ArticleTitle>An unusual cause of acute abdomen: torsion of colonic duplication over a duplicated appendix.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>722-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 2-year old boy with torsion of colonic duplication, which had a proximal communication with the cecum via an incomplete duplicated appendix, is presented. The clinical picture and complications of this rare association are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
